{title: Amazing Grace}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
A[G]mazing grace, how [G7]sweet the [C]sound, that [G]saved a wretch like [D]me.
I [G]once was [G7]lost, but [C]now am [G]found, was [Em]blind, but [D]now I [G]see.

{c: Verse 2}
'Twas [G]grace that [G7]taught my [C]heart to [G]fear, and [D]grace my fears re[D]lieved.
How [G]precious [G7]did that [C]grace ap[G]pear, the [Em]hour I [D]first be[G]lieved.

{c: Verse 3}
Through [G]many [G7]dangers, [C]toils and [G]snares, I [D]have already [D]come.
'Tis [G]grace hath [G7]brought me [C]safe thus [G]far, and [Em]grace will [D]lead me [G]home.
